    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d343">

                <pb facs="0684" n="560" xml:id="pg560"/>

                <head>No. 339.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoppin to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 21, 1881</date>.
                        (Received December 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 223.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy of the correspondence between this legation and the foreign office in
                    relation to the interference, by inhabitants of Newfoundland, with fishermen of
                    the United States, which was referred to in your dispatch to Mr. Lowell, No.
                    206, of the 30th of July last, and which you instructed him to bring to the
                    attention of Her Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. J. HOPPIN.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d343-a1.xml" xpointer="d343-a1"/>
